# Title: Potentially Suspicious Execution Of Regasm/Regsvcs From Uncommon Location
# ID: cc368ed0-2411-45dc-a222-510ace303cb2
# Status: test
# Level: medium
# Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
# Date: 2022-08-25
# Tags: attack.stealth, attack.t1218.009
# Description: Detects potentially suspicious execution of the Regasm/Regsvcs utilities from a potentially suspicious location
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

index=* eventtype=wineventlog (((process_exec="*\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\*" OR process_exec="*\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Start Menu\\Programs\\Startup\\*" OR process_exec="*\\PerfLogs\\*" OR process_exec="*\\Users\\Public\\*" OR process_exec="*\\Windows\\Temp\\*")) AND (((process_path="*\\Regsvcs.exe" OR process_path="*\\Regasm.exe")) OR ((process_name="RegSvcs.exe" OR process_name="RegAsm.exe"))))
